Author: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 11:28:30 2026 +0200

    fix(pi-cache-optimizer): require a declared wire format before giving DeepSeek compat advice
    
    The cache optimizer treated a substring match on the model id as evidence that a
    channel spoke DeepSeek's reasoning wire format. Every DeepSeek-named model behind
    any OpenAI-compatible proxy was told its compat lacked thinkingFormat and
    requiresReasoningContentOnAssistantMessages, and the fix command would write
    thinkingFormat into models.json on that basis. A model name is not protocol
    evidence, and that write is a wire-format switch rather than a cache flag.
    
    Applicability now comes from an explicit declared thinkingFormat, through one gate
    every DeepSeek-specific check asks first. The flag that gates the check is never
    itself reported as missing, because demanding it would be circular. Session
    affinity moved to the generic proxy path and keeps its explicit-false opt-out, so
    an operator whose proxy rejects custom headers can say so once.
    
    models.json states the two facts about the gateway channel that were previously
    inferred: session-affinity support on the provider, and text plus image input on
    the DeepSeek entry, which stops that channel silently dropping images.
    
    Authored by another session in this repository, not by this one. Committed here on
    the operator's instruction after reading every diff, running the suite (114 tests,
    114 passing) and scanning the probe evidence for credentials. Its spec packet was
    uncommitted and ships alongside the code rather than leaving the change undocumented.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UpKZsFWY5kjNhTnMSaXoov

